  "design": {
    "decision": "Bid higher, because about two sure losers become near-sure winners and the team sees this before bidding. It also changes how much [2]s are worth in the shop.",
    "opponent": "Revealed the first time a converted [A] wins. Opponents face extra [A]s and can only answer by voiding the suit and trumping.",
    "rationale": "The brief asks for large, visible hand changes with better destinations. This changes only the team's worst cards, while the random cb-become-ace can pick a card that is already an [A], so this turns more losers into winners than a random change of the same size. It costs Nil and Low Cards builds their [2]s, which is a real tension.",
